ational space  station late last night  the landing wraps up an ambitious test  of the first manned  private spacecraft which launched in may  still ahead the triggers behind  america's gun sales surge  during the pandemic  you're watching global national  gun sales across the united states have  reached record highs  since the pandemic began in some states  shops selling these weapons are  considered an essential service  and even when other states tried to shut  them down they were still the internet  as reggie chichini reports a growing  number of buyers  are first-time gun owners as more  americans find themselves sinking under  the fear of the unknown  millions have sought safety in the palm  of their hands  it started with kovid and now it's  the riots pandemic panic has triggered a  rush on gun purchases since the  beginning of the year and data shows  it's not gun aficionados looking to arm  themselves  forty percent of gun sales were to first  time buyers  i've been wanting to do this for a while  but this is kind of like the tipping  point where  i need to protect myself roughly 14  million background checks were conducted  between march  and june june alone saw a 136 percent  increase from the previous year  these are the highest numbers in the  fbi's background check program  22 year history it might be something  that produces disorder  or perceived as disorder it might be the  black lives matter demonstrations  and counter demonstrations by the  beginning of the summer  gun permits in georgia tripled from 2019  and doubled in oklahoma new york  illinois and minnesota  sales of handguns are outpacing long  guns two to one  it's linked to self-protection it's it's  survival related  and while some criminologists say bursts  of sales are not generally followed by  increased gun violence  gun control advocates disagree gun  violence is a public health  epidemic buying a gun will not make you  safer now  nor in the future the economic situation  in the u.s 